    isbefore: []  # f3a6
    duplicate_of: []  # f3a6
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f3a6
    pr_ref:  # f3a6
    description: "Found by the Fundamental Concept Audit of `edge.meta['call_construct']`\n(2026-08-20). AST inventory: 107 producer sites, 14 distinct values.\n\nINV-vakaf drained exactly ONE instance of this field's axis-mixing — the\n`cross_file` locality value on bash/objc — and split it into the new\n`call_locality` key per the 2026-06-25 human ruling. Four values of the SAME\nmechanic were left in the field. Per the audit playbook's \"one leak is never\nalone\", they are filed together here.\n\n**The four, with the leakage test each fails:**\n\n1. `remote_external` (erlang.py:540) vs `remote` (erlang.py:523).\n   IDENTICAL AST shape — both are `mod:func(args)`. Read the code: `remote`\n   is the `if lookup_result.found` branch; `remote_external` is the `else`\n   branch, which mints a synthetic external node. The ONLY difference is\n   whether the resolver found the callee. FAILS Test 1 (property\n   derivability): derivable from `Edge.is_resolved` / the dst.\n\n2. `application_external` (haskell.py:551) vs `application` (haskell.py:524).\n   Identical structure, identical cause — the unresolved branch minting an\n   external node. FAILS Test 1.\n\n3. `chained_return_type` (go.py:2702). Names HOW the receiver type was\n   resolved (chained through a call's return type). The call is syntactically\n   a method call. FAILS Test 4 (mechanism vs category). Fold target:\n   `resolution_quality`, which exists for exactly this (\"names uncertainty in\n   the resolution pathway\").\n\n4. `interface_dispatch` (go.py:2855,2857). Names the dispatch mechanism — the\n   call resolved to an interface method rather than a concrete impl. FAILS\n   Test 4. Fold target: the sibling key `mechanism`, whose own MetaKeySpec\n   says it \"names HOW the dispatch/call is wired\".\n\nValues 1 and 2 are the ADR-0028 cluster-28B shape (resolution status leaking\ninto a non-resolution field) reproduced one field over.\n\n**Values adjudicated and KEPT** (recorded so a later audit does not re-litigate):\n`local` vs `remote` in erlang is a GENUINE syntactic distinction (bare atom\ncall vs `mod:`-qualified) and does NOT mean same-file — the local branch still\nresolves cross-file via import hints, so it does not collide with\n`call_locality`. `method` / `function` / `constructor` / `pipe` / `application`\n/ `macro_body` are on-axis.\n\n**UNMEASURED consequence — do not treat as a finding.** Every consumer of\n`call_construct` tests it against exactly one value, `== \"method\"`\n(io_boundary.py:507,874; taint.py:1891; verify_claims.py:1755). Three of the 14\nvalues denote syntactic method calls (`method`, `interface_dispatch`,\n`chained_return_type`) but only one matches that gate, so the F3 method refusal\nmay fail open on the other two. INV-nizom is the same invariant with the\nopposite cause (cpp stamps NOTHING, so the gate is unconditional there).\n**Per INV-linub's standing directive, any such claim must be measured through\nL4 on FINDINGS, not on edges** — a capability measured at the analyzer is not\nrecall. That measurement has NOT been run and is the first task under this item.\n\n**Coverage caveat on the inventory.** The edge-family attribution covered 95 of\n107 sites. 12 sites bind the meta dict to a variable before passing it, so they\nare invisible to both grep and to a check that reads the constructor call —\nincluding BOTH `interface_dispatch` sites, four `py.py` `method` sites, plus\nscala.py, swift.py, rust.py and the shared `analyze/base.py:898` helper. The\nvalue taxonomy above is complete; the edge_type attribution is not."  # f3a6
    fields:  # f3a6
      statement: "Every value of edge.meta.call_construct names the source-language syntactic call construct and nothing else, so a consumer reads the construct without decoding resolution status or dispatch mechanism."  # f3a6
      root_cause: "INV-vakaf split only the cross_file locality value out of this field (bash/objc, into the new call_locality key). Four values of the same mechanic remain. erlang remote_external (erlang.py:540) and haskell application_external (haskell.py:551) differ from their siblings remote/application ONLY by whether the resolver lookup succeeded, being the else-branch that mints a synthetic external node, which is resolution status derivable from Edge.is_resolved and the dst. go chained_return_type (go.py:2702) names how the receiver type was resolved, not the call syntax. go interface_dispatch (go.py:2855,2857) names the dispatch mechanism, for which the sibling meta key named mechanism already exists."  # f3a6
