- op: discuss  # e9e9
  at: '2026-08-20T21:11:38Z'  # e9e9
  by: agent  # e9e9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e9e9
  clock: 3  # e9e9
  nonce: e9e9  # e9e9
  message: "COVERAGE GAP CLOSED, same day (2026-08-20). The description's caveat -- 'edge-family attribution covered 95 of 107 sites; the value taxonomy is complete, the edge_type attribution is not' -- is now RESOLVED. A second AST pass with intra-procedural tracking (per-scope map from local name to the call_construct literals bound to it, via dict literal, ternary-of-dicts, and subscript assign, then matching Edge.create sites whose meta= is that name) attributed 105 distinct (file, line, value) sites. The 12 previously-unattributed sites were not a coverage hole: they are the DEFINITION lines where the dict or variable is built, and the resolver reports each at its Edge.create line instead (go.py:2855 and :2857 define the ternary, go.py:2859 emits). Same sites, different line. RESULTS. Both values I could not previously attribute land on calls edges and are NOT edge-family breaches: interface_dispatch (go.py:2859) edge_type=calls, chained_return_type (go.py:2694) edge_type=calls. Same for remote_external (erlang.py:532) and application_external (haskell.py:538), both calls. So the four fold candidates in this item are all correctly on the call family; their defect is purely the axis-mixing named in root_cause, not misplacement. The breach count is therefore 7 and is now a TOTAL, not a floor: 5 constructor-on-instantiates (canonical, ruled under WI-toruz) and 2 method_group-on-references (genuine misfile, WI-diruk). ONE FALSE POSITIVE ADJUDICATED AND KEPT, recorded so a future checker does not refile it: py.py:5939 emits edge_type as a ternary and meta as a second ternary COUPLED ON THE SAME CONDITION (_is_ctor), so call_construct is present only on the calls branch and absent on the instantiates branch. That is correct and deliberate per WI-jubag. Any automated edge-family gate written for this axis must evaluate the coupled condition rather than flag a dynamic edge_type."  # e9e9
- op: discuss  # 6633
  at: '2026-08-20T21:13:26Z'  # 6633
  by: agent  # 6633
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6633
  clock: 4  # 6633
  nonce: '6633'  # 6633
  message: "GAP 2 RESOLVED STRUCTURALLY, NOT BY A/B (2026-08-20). The description flags an UNMEASURED consequence -- that go interface_dispatch and chained_return_type, being syntactic method calls that do not equal the string 'method', might fail the F3 method refusal OPEN. Read end to end, that hypothesis is very likely VACUOUS by construction, so the A/B INV-linub would require is not worth running as specified. WHY. The F3 refusal at taint.py:1891 sits behind 'if not qualified', and qualified is computed at taint.py:1888 as module = _module_from_symbol_path(edge dst), then fq = module.callee_name. The gate is therefore reached only when the DST yields no derivable module -- _module_from_symbol_path returns empty string for the 'external' placeholder, which is the documented INV-finoh untyped-receiver case. But both suspect values are stamped ONLY on edges whose dst is an in-repo RESOLVED symbol: go.py:2859 sets dst=_iface_candidate.id drawn from global_symbols, and go.py:2702 sets dst=target.id drawn from global_symbols[outer_qualified]. Those dsts carry real paths, so they take the qualified branch and never reach the refusal. More basically, an edge resolving to a first-party Go interface method is not a candidate for I/O-primitive catalogue matching at all -- that machinery matches EXTERNAL primitives. RESIDUAL CONDITION, stated rather than hidden: the hypothesis would need an edge that BOTH carries one of these two values (implying an in-repo resolved dst) AND reaches the no-module gate (requiring no derivable module). Those are contradictory unless an in-repo Go symbol id yields an empty module slot -- e.g. a malformed or path-less symbol id. That is the only surviving way in, and it is a different defect (id construction, ADR-0034/0036 territory) rather than a call_construct one. NOT EXECUTED: this is a structural read of the emit sites and the gate precondition, not a live run. It is falsifiable by finding one go edge carrying either value whose dst has an empty module slot. Recorded so the next agent does not spend a Go-corpus A/B on a contradiction."  # 6633
