- op: discuss  # c5c8
  at: '2026-08-21T01:01:27Z'  # c5c8
  by: agent  # c5c8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c5c8
  clock: 6  # c5c8
  nonce: c5c8  # c5c8
  message: "SATISFIED. Merged 9db326c416 (auto-pr rebased; verified by CONTENT on origin/dev -- 0 emit sites remain for remote_external, application_external, chained_return_type, interface_dispatch under call_construct). All four values drained, each to the axis it was actually naming: erlang remote_external -> remote and haskell application_external -> application (the suffix marked only whether the resolver found the callee, which is already recoverable from dst -- synthetic external node id vs in-repo symbol id -- and the AST shape is identical either way); go chained_return_type -> call_construct=method + resolution_quality=chained_return_type (a resolution MECHANISM); go interface_dispatch -> call_construct=method. ONE FOLD TARGET IN THIS ITEM'S OWN DESCRIPTION WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED. The description proposed moving interface_dispatch to meta['mechanism']. Reading the emit site showed the same Edge.create ALREADY passes evidence_type='interface_dispatch' -- a registered inference pathway meaning 'edge inferred from interface-method dispatch resolution'. So one value was stated TWICE on two different axes of a single edge, and moving it to a third key would have relocated the duplicate instead of removing it. Behaviourally free: that evidence type has base_confidence=None, so the edge keeps its explicit 0.75/0.5 and disambiguation_fallback is untouched. GUARDED WITH A POSITIVE CONTROL: a live-tree AST walk asserts no producer emits any of the four (AST and not grep, because a regex over source also matches its own docstrings and the fold comments name every folded value), plus a second test pointing the SAME walk at 'method' -- an assertion over an empty search passes just as happily when the walk is broken, so the control is what makes the guard evidence. VERIFICATION: 11856 passed, 100% coverage, mypy ratchet clean, 16/16 pre-commit gates (ruff caught a zip-without-strict in the new guard and blocked the first commit attempt). No consumer affected -- every reader of call_construct tests it against the single literal 'method' and none of the four had a reader; the one test asserting remote_external and the one test DOCSTRING describing it were both updated."  # c5c8
